        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix(meeting-bot): avoid stale state during transcript and browser recovery",
        "body": "Related: #109755\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes three deferred meeting-bot reliability issues: transcript cursor polling could replay retained lines under shifted indices after a page gap, untargeted browser recovery could choose a Google sign-in tab before an active meeting tab, and talkback could report ready before microphone state was known.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nTranscript retention now exposes one contiguous cursor segment and drops a disconnected prefix when page-local history advances. Untargeted recovery prefers adapter-normalized meeting URLs over login fallbacks. Browser-managed local and paired-node talkback now require an explicit unmuted observation; unknown microphone state is transiently blocked as browser-unverified, matching the stricter Teams meetings policy. The documented `chrome.launch: false` externally managed bridge mode remains unchanged.\n\n## User Impact\n\nCursor-polling clients no longer receive old transcript lines again after retention gaps. Meeting recovery chooses a real call over a sign-in fallback when both exist. Bots do not claim speech readiness or start realtime audio while microphone state is unknown.\n\n## Evidence\n\n- Added same-epoch and epoch-change transcript gap regressions; 10 focused meeting-bot tests pass.\n- Added login-first untargeted recovery regression; 7 Chrome transport tests pass.\n- Added unknown-microphone runtime plus paired-node muted, unknown, unmuted, retry, and externally managed regressions; 160 Google Meet tests pass.\n- Teams sibling proof: 72 tests pass.\n- Fresh post-review autoreview: no findings, patch correct at 0.90 confidence.\n- Full changed-surface Testbox gate passed after the paired-node fix: format, API and dependency guards, four typecheck lanes, core and extension lint, runtime guards. Blacksmith Testbox `tbx_01kxrjgqsnjs3p2cejvd235ay5`; run https://github.com/openclaw/openclaw/actions/runs/29600815747.\n\nLive signed-in Meet/audio validation was not available in this checkout; the browser-facing contracts are covered by focused integration tests.\n",
